::'''March 7th:''' Am I? I feel pretty normal. Anyway, this case has really got my detective blood pumping. I need to get to the bottom of it...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're in high spirits today.
::'''March 7th:''' Yup! I always dreamed of a head-scratcher like this &mdash; a chance to showcase my detective genius.
:'''March 7th:''' I've been familiarizing myself with The Angler Mystery lately. &mdash; I think it's safe to say I have the best investigative mind on the Express at this point...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The Angler Mystery?
:'''Jingyan:''' You have good taste, Miss March. The Angler Mystery is a classic detective novel on the Xianzhou... I read it when I was young and dreamed about working in the Commission ever since.
:'''Jingyan:''' I didn't think it would be attracting new readers more than 200 years later.
:'''March 7th:''' *gasp* A fellow reader! But Miss Jingyan, the author &mdash; Su Fang &mdash; was the lead medical assistant in an apothecary, and the main character &mdash; the Angler &mdash; is a healer... Why didn't you want to join the Alchemy Commission instead?
:'''Jingyan:''' *sigh* A number of reasons. This job may be trivial, but I have my reasons for being here... Plus, hehe, the threshold for the Alchemy Commission was too difficult for me to reach.
:'''March 7th:''' I see... But your lives are so long &mdash; shouldn't career change be easy?
:'''Jingyan:''' I considered it once... That was a long time ago. The longer I stay in this job, the more I understand its purpose. Fighting crime, helping the weak, solving the problems no one wants to touch... It's a satisfying feeling.
:'''March 7th:''' Wow, good for you Miss Jingyan.
:'''Welt:''' Sounds like you really care.

;(Talk to Welt Yang)
